capabilities.behavior:
Retrieval from the search index returns spans. The generator (local or cloud, as the rights gate allows) must return schema-validated structured output. A deterministic post-validator then checks three things:
- each quote equals the source text at its offsets;
- every numeric token in a claim appears in a cited span after unit and scale normalization;
- entities resolve.
Claims that fail are marked 'unsupported' and hidden by default. Multi-document mode is limited by a configurable document count and token budget. A summary is invalidated when one of its sources changes version. Document text is untrusted: instructions embedded in it cannot change tools, limits or routing (Ch 19/23). Paid calls stay disabled until the owner sets a budget, and local models are used otherwise. The system abstains when retrieval confidence is low. Outputs are labelled AI-generated.
